From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:39:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt8781-zinwa-q25: Keep VBIF28 on

The bootloader enables VBIF28 and MediaTek's board files keep it always
on; nothing in the board description consumes it, so the regulator core
would switch it off as unused. Mark it always-on as the vendor DT does.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
index 7cd6ce07..ec02b3c4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
@@ -488,6 +488,7 @@
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <2800000>;
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <2800000>;
 				regulator-enable-ramp-delay = <270>;
+				regulator-always-on;
 			};
 
 			mt6366_vsram_proc12_reg: vsram-proc12 {
